<GuideLayout 
  title="How to Scale Your Brand with Influencer Marketing" 
  type="MARKETING"
  description="Discover how to partner with fitness influencers to drive brand awareness and sales for your new activewear collection."
>
  <h2>The Era of Social Influence</h2>
  <p>In the fitness industry, trust is the primary currency. Consumers no longer look at traditional ads; they look at the athletes and influencers they follow for product recommendations.</p>
  
  <h3>Identifying the Right Partners</h3>
  <p>Don't just chase follower counts. Look for 'Nano' and 'Micro' influencers (5k-50k followers) who have high engagement rates and a dedicated community. Their recommendation often carries more weight than a celebrity with millions of passive followers.</p>

  <h3>Campaign Strategies</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Product Gifting:</strong> Send your latest collection to influencers for honest reviews.</li>
    <li><strong>Affiliate Programs:</strong> Provide unique discount codes to track sales and reward influencers with commissions.</li>
    <li><strong>Content Collaboration:</strong> Co-create workout videos or "A Day in the Life" content featuring your brand.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Measuring ROI</h3>
  <p>Use UTM parameters and dedicated landing pages to track where your traffic is coming from. Focus on 'Cost Per Acquisition' (CPA) rather than just impressions.</p>
</GuideLayout>
